description:
In the refactored Fragment::from_bytes, the old code had two separate checks:

```rust
if data.len() != TILE_SIZE + 2 {
    return Err(FragmentError::InvalidTileLength);
}
if window == 1 && fcn == 0 {
    return Err(FragmentError::InvalidFcn);
}
```

The new code (fragment.rs:182) combines them into:

```rust
} else if data.len() != TILE_SIZE + 2 || (window == 1 && fcn == 0) {
    return Err(FragmentError::InvalidTileLength);
}
```

When window==1 and fcn==0, the caller now gets InvalidTileLength instead of InvalidFcn. This loses error granularity and is inconsistent with Fragment::write_to which returns InvalidFcn for the same condition (line 141).
